+# LeCun "World Models" 2026 — Verified Citation Collection + Carnot Mapping
+
+**Purpose.** A curated quote bank from Yann LeCun's 2026 world-models talks (the ETH Zürich
+"Frontiers of Embodied AI" talk, video: https://youtu.be/72Xj8k5WQX4, and the Brown University
+Lemley Lecture of 2026-04-02 covering the same material) plus the AMI Labs launch coverage.
+Assembled for citation in paper-v6 positioning and the operator's external writing — this is the
+strongest external validation yet of the EBM/world-model lineage Carnot builds on, from the
+lineage's originator, AND it names the exact open problem (hierarchical planning) where Carnot has
+fresh empirical micro-scale data.
+
+**Provenance / verification discipline.** Carnot cannot transcribe the video directly. Every quote
+below was captured 2026-06-10 from PRESS COVERAGE of the lectures via WebFetch; quotes appearing
+verbatim-identical in BOTH the Brown Daily Herald and Brown University News writeups are marked
+**[VERIFIED-2SRC]**; single-source quotes are **[1SRC — re-check against the video/transcript
+before paper use]**. Per the literature-priority discipline, diff any quote against the primary
+video transcript before it appears in a published artifact.
+
+---
+
+## Source A — Brown University News (2026-04-01/02 Lemley Lecture)
+
+- URL: https://www.brown.edu/news/2026-04-01/yann-lecun-artificial-intelligence-pioneer
+- Accessed: 2026-06-10
+
+### A1. The agentic-prediction gap [1SRC] — THE quote for Carnot's verifier-validated acting
+> "The result is that everybody these days in AI is talking about agentic systems — systems that
+> can produce actions in the world — and almost none of those systems at the moment are capable of
+> predicting the outcome… of their actions. It's a very bad way to produce an action… if you're
+> not able to predict the consequences of it. In fact, it might be dangerous."
+
+### A2. World-model definition [1SRC]
+> "A world model is a predictive system that, given the current state of the world… and given an
+> action that you imagine taking, [you can] predict the next state of the world that will result
+> from this action or intervention. If you have such a world model that predicts what the world is
+> going to be after you take an action, you can use that for planning."
+
+### A3. On LLM-scaling investment [1SRC]
+> "There's literally hundreds of billions invested in an industry that basically is counting on
+> the fact that LLMs [are] going to reach human-level intelligence. It's complete BS."
+
+### A4. On current systems [VERIFIED-2SRC for the final sentence]
+> "AI sucks. We have systems that can manipulate language, and they fool us into thinking they are
+> smart because they manipulate language. But in fact, they are completely helpless when it comes
+> to the physical world."
+
+## Source B — Brown Daily Herald (same lecture)
+
+- URL: https://www.browndailyherald.com/article/2026/04/ai-pioneer-yann-lecun-discusses-new-frontiers-in-the-field-at-brown-lecture
+- Accessed: 2026-06-10
+
+### B1. Hierarchical planning — the named open problem [1SRC]
+> "Here is the big secret of AI: Nobody knows how to do hierarchical planning."
+
+### B2. The slide [1SRC — reported as red-caps slide text]
+> "IF YOU ARE INTERESTED IN HUMAN-LEVEL AI, DON'T WORK ON LLMs."
+
+### B3. Intelligence definition [1SRC]
+> "The ability to accomplish new tasks you've never been exposed to and solve new problems without
+> any prior training."
+
+## Source C — AMI Labs launch context
+
+- AIwire (2026-03-11): AMI raised a ~$1B seed to build "foundational world models";
+  https://www.hpcwire.com/aiwire/2026/03/11/yann-lecuns-ami-secures-1b-seed-to-develop-ai-world-models/
+- MIT Technology Review (2026-01-22): AMI as "a contrarian bet against large language models";
+  https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/01/22/1131661/yann-lecuns-new-venture-ami-labs/
+- AMI's stated pillars (per launch coverage): systems that understand the world, have persistent
+  memory, can reason and plan, and are controllable and safe.
+
+---
+
+## Carnot mapping (why these quotes are load-bearing)
+
+1. **A1 ↔ verifier-validated acting.** Carnot's ARC-AGI-3 results are an existence proof at micro
+   scale of exactly what A1 demands: the r11l L1→L3 advance (exp3992) re-induces each level's rule
+   and uses the GAP-4 execution verifier to validate the candidate rule against held-out
+   transitions BEFORE committing the action sequence. Predicting consequences before acting is not
+   aspiration here; it is the measured mechanism that broke the L2 wall.
+
+2. **A2 ↔ executable world models.** Carnot's induced world models are `transform/predict`
+   PROGRAMS with exact execution verification (demo-fit gates, content-hash matching,
+   consistency energy on held-out transitions) — discrete and mechanically checkable where
+   JEPA-style models are continuous and learned. Differentiated, ownable position.
+
+3. **The EBM caution Carnot's data adds.** The GAP-3 program adversarially confirmed (4 rounds,
+   5/5 each) that LEARNED scorers — confidence scalars, latents, trained content-energies — are
+   vote-shadows or statistically random on real ARC candidates. What reached the headroom was
+   program induction + execution consistency. Refinement of the energy thesis: the energy must be
+   GROUNDED (executable / constraint-checked), not a trained discriminator. "The energy function
+   is ground truth, it cannot be gamed" — Carnot's invariant — is the version of LeCun's bet that
+   survived our adversarial gauntlet.
+
+4. **B1 ↔ the measured planning wall.** Carnot's vc33 finding: a 99%-accurate, verifier-certified
+   world model STILL failed to solve the game — goal induction + Sokoban-class planning is a
+   separate unsolved layer above dynamics (17/25 ARC-3 games sit behind it; the r11l L4 wall is
+   where our per-level baby-hierarchical loop stops). Empirical micro-confirmation of B1, with
+   honest numbers — a contribution venue, not just agreement.
+
+5. **AMI pillars ↔ Carnot tracks.** Persistent memory ↔ ArcMemo (2,668→17→10 action transfers);
+   reason/plan ↔ the induce→verify→act loop; controllable-and-safe ↔ verifier-as-gate (a concrete
+   mechanism where the talk is abstract). Strategic note: $1B validates the Phase-3 market thesis
+   AND raises subsumption risk; Carnot's defensible ground remains the grounded-verifier moat +
+   decentralization/sovereignty (local-first, open weights vs. venture-backed closed development).
+
+**Paper-v6 usage note.** Quote A1/A2/B1 in positioning; pair B1 with the vc33/L4-wall numbers;
+pair the EBM caution (point 3) with the GAP-3 ledger. Per the narrowing discipline, do NOT imply
+LeCun endorses Carnot — the claim is independent convergence on the architecture class plus our
+execution-grounding refinement and micro-scale evidence.
